ull,"mana_cost":"{4}{W}{W}","name":"Yosei, the Morning Star","oracle_id":"5c2d0ead-8bfc-4ca7-9b38-2fc07af1c1d5","oracle_text":"Flying\nWhen Yosei dies, target player skips their next untap step. Tap up to five target permanents that player controls.","power":"5","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2017-11-17","toughness":"5","type_line":"Legendary Creature — Dragon Spirit"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If a permanent won't untap during its controller's next untap step, that effect waits to apply until its controller has an untap step that isn't skipped.","oracle_id":"5c2d0ead-8bfc-4ca7-9b38-2fc07af1c1d5","published_at":"2017-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If all of the permanents targeted by Yosei's ability become illegal targets, nothing becomes tapped, but the target player still skips their untap step.","oracle_id":"5c2d0ead-8bfc-4ca7-9b38-2fc07af1c1d5","published_at":"2017-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If any of the targets of Yosei's ability are illegal, they won't be tapped.","oracle_id":"5c2d0ead-8bfc-4ca7-9b38-2fc07af1c1d5","published_at":"2017-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If more than one effect instructs a player to skip their next untap step, such as if Yosei dies more than once in a turn, that player skips that many untap steps. This is different from effects that state that something doesn't untap during an untap step.","oracle_id":"5c2d0ead-8bfc-4ca7-9b38-2fc07af1c1d5","published_at":"2017-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the player becomes an illegal target, the target permanents are tapped, but the player doesn't skip their untap step.","oracle_id":"5c2d0ead-8bfc-4ca7-9b38-2fc07af1c1d5","published_at":"2017-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If more than one Stonehorn Dignitary enters the battlefield and their abilities target the same opponent, that opponent will skip that many combat phases (over multiple turns if necessary). Skipping one combat phase won't satisfy all of the effects.","oracle_id":"65368569-68bf-4498-9979-d2935942ca49","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once a combat phase starts, it can't be skipped. A Stonehorn Dignitary entering the battlefield during combat won't affect that combat, even if it's the turn of the opponent chosen as the target of the triggered ability.","oracle_id":"65368569-68bf-4498-9979-d2935942ca49","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you are damaged by more than one, the effects are cumulative and you skip multiple combat phases.","oracle_id":"cb479ce1-59e8-4531-9a21-f7c97d334817","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The owner of a card is the player who started the game with that card in their deck.","oracle_id":"cb8ec2e4-8223-4172-8f2c-37c918a573fa","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The owner of a token is the player under whose control the token was put onto the battlefield.","oracle_id":"cb8ec2e4-8223-4172-8f2c-37c918a573fa","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You skip one turn as part of the effect.","oracle_id":"f79f84c9-2023-4348-863b-a3b4bc382904","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
